 "source_notes": "All values from the Bowen National Research PDF (single source; no news/interactive pages used), read via WebFetch text extraction. (1) rental_gap/forsale_gap/total_gap + gap_to_*_pct: table 'Housing Gaps by Tenure and County - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)', pp. II-14 to II-16; columns: Rental Housing Gap [Total Rental Gap | Share of State | Gap to Renter Households Ratio], For-Sale Housing Gap [Total For-Sale Gap | Share of State | Gap to Owner Households Ratio], Total Housing Gap [Total Gap | Share of State | Gap to Total Households Ratio]. Ratios use 2029 projected households by tenure. State Total row: 322,360 / 442,118 / 764,478 (21.2% / 14.3% / 16.6%). (2) households_2024/2029, hh_growth_pct: table 'Total Households', pp. III-22 to III-23; columns: 2010 Census | 2020 Census | Change 2010-2020 (Number, Percent) | 2024 Estimated | Change 2020-2024 (Number, Percent) | 2029 Projected | Change 2024-2029 (Number, Percent). hh_growth_pct = the printed 'Change 2024-2029 Percent'. State: 4,384,359 -> 4,602,519, 5.0%. (3) rental_gap_by_ami: table 'Overall Rental Housing Gaps - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)', pp. V-5 to V-7; columns are Percent of Area Median Income: <30% | 31%-50% | 51%-80% | 81%-120% | 121%-150% | 151%+ | Total Units | Share of State | Gap to Renter Household Ratio. (4) forsale_gap_by_price: table 'Overall For-Sale Housing Gaps - State of North Carolina (2024 to 2029)', pp. V-13 to V-15; SAME AMI bands as rental (keys are AMI bands, not dollar prices). County-specific dollar price ranges per band exist only in Addendum A ('[COUNTY] COUNTY Housing Gap Estimates by Income (2024 to 2029)') and were NOT extracted. (5) multifamily_vacancy_pct: table 'Surveyed Multifamily Rental Housing Supply by County', pp. IV-4 to IV-5, column 'Overall Vacancy Rate' (all surveyed market-rate + Tax Credit + government-subsidized projects). null = report shows 0 projects surveyed and dashes (no data, not 0% vacancy). mf_projects_surveyed / mf_units_surveyed from same table. (6) forsale_availability_pct, median_list_price, forsale_available_units: table 'Available For-Sale Housing by County' (as of early July 2024), pp. IV-36 to IV-38; columns: Total Available Units | % Share of State Total | Availability Rate | Average List Price | Median List Price | Average Days on Market | Average Year Built. Checks passed for all 26 counties: rental+forsale=total; AMI bands sum to rental and for-sale totals; printed hh growth % matches 2024/2029 counts; vacancy % matches vacant/total units.",
